  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Activity under preparation Establishment of an ACP Trust Fund for private sector operations under EFSD+</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Council Decision (EU) 2020/2233 on the use of the Africa, Caribbean and Pacific (ACP) Investment Facility (IF) reflows, adopted unanimously on 23 December 2020, approved the transfer of the IF reflows as contributions to NDICI Global Europe and will be governed under EFSD+. The Council Decision also mentions: &amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;i) &amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;the earmarking of the ACP IF reflows for ACP countries, &amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;ii) &amp;nbsp;the EIB&#xbf;s role as the implementing entity without business interruption in the ACP countries,&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;iii) their nature as external assigned revenues and therefore a top up of current MFF resources.&amp;nbsp;The ACP Trust Fund is to be managed by the EIB under the EFSD+ governance and will focus on high risk, impact finance operations and investments, including equity, quasi-equity, subordinated debt, risk-sharing, local currency lending and lending with particular focus to Least Developed Countries (LDC) and countries in fragile situations. The objectives are in the line with the SDGs and NDICI-Global Europe regulation in general and contribute to overarching EU policy objectives, e.g. Green Deal, Global Gateway, gender equality, jobs and inclusive growth. &amp;nbsp;The ACP Trust Fund will follow a policy-first approach aligned with the NDICI-Global Europe programming documents. It will promote sustainable private sector driven and inclusive green economic growth and development, especially in Least Developed Countries and Fragile States. In addition it will also incentivise and support clients/ promoters to design and implement projects that aim to achieve positive social and environmental impacts such as, but not limited to, environmental sustainability, climate change mitigation and adaptation, gender equality, social inclusion, social cohesion and economic resilience.&amp;nbsp;The ACP Trust Fund operations will seek maximum additionality and complementarity by offering in particular those financing tools as the former Impact Financing Envelope under the ACP IF.&amp;nbsp;</narrative>
  </description>
